sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — Morphometric validation: 51/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "What exists now: Law 3's convergence is a real numerical validation against an independent closed form (error 2.5e-5 at N = 240, O(h^2)); Law 1's BVP is checked against its continuum limit (31.51 vs 32.01, 1.6 %) and the Hill form is now fitted with a quantified residual (3.05 cells RMS) rather than asserted (+1); Law 4's slope change is a measured property of the generator; Law 6's basin fraction (0 -> 1) and conditioning response (0.0015 -> 1.0) are non-identity outcomes; Delta E = -eta N^2 is labelled an identity; Law 7's Delta CP values are pinned to a hash-verified committed artefact; the Law 2 isolation ratio e^10 and the Law 8 bond fractions were re-derived. The written record of the validation now matches the computed values in the criteria doc, YAML and KG verified_laws (+8 restored). Deductions: no measurement is compared with a value measured on an organism, an experiment or a figure in any cited paper - Chvykov 2021's measured enrichment, Pigozzi 2025's conditioning success, Cervera 2020's voltage levels and Pietak 2016's BETSE gradients all exist and none is used (-30); the Law 3 G_gj spread, the Law 8 threshold comparisons and the new Law 1 RMS assertion are same-expression or cannot-fail checks (-8); the builder still ships no measurements sidecar of its own, and the KG payload's `verified_measurements` is the referee's Pass 3 sidecar with two entries rewritten by the builder under the referee's meas_ids (-8); the CE2 reference is repository-internal (-4)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L600–L675: verified_measurements: 24 entries carrying this referee's Pass 3 meas_ids. m1 (L602-L616) still says '918-line script' and cites L177-L225 / L231-L277; m2 (L617-L631) cites 'MathOfBiology.lean L1200-L1375', a section that does not exist in the committed file (956 lines). m4 (L647-L660) and m5 (L662-L675) were rewritten by the builder (13 -> 17 'entries_of_18'; 7 -> 0 'All 7 Pass 3.1 discrepancies reconciled in Pass 3.2') while the referee's own sidecar for the same meas_ids still read 13 and 7 at the time. Builder-authored values under referee identifiers <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json#L600-L675>",
            "models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py L848–L850: Law 1 assertions: reach(G_gj = 0) = 1, reach(WT) > reach(G_gj = 0), fitted RMS < unfitted RMS. The first two are on the BVP; the third cannot fail. A tolerance check against the continuum 31.51 or on the fitted RMS itself would be a validation and is not made <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9987ff10/models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py#L848-L850>" ;
        pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-catalog-verification-cited-video-ids-resolving-in-the-374-video-catalog-with-sha-256-pin>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-cli-expressivity-model-flags-that-complete-a-self-test-run-with-a-non-default-value>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-bvp-spatial-reach-at-g-gj-1-0-n-100-g-half-0-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-hill-form-1-n-1-g-g-g-eff-fitted-to-the-bvp-reach-curve-over-g-in-0-2-51-points-g-eff-and-rms-residual>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-bell-conductance-isolation-ratio-g-60-60-g-10-10-at-v-th-35-v-0-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-healthy-tail-v-mem-bell-gated-vs-ohmic-control-t-80>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-absolute-error-of-c-post-c-ant-vs-exp-dv-v-t-across-n-ap-15-30-60-120-240>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-central-difference-c-post-c-ant-at-dv-40-mv-n-ap-120-g-gj-1-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-spread-of-c-post-c-ant-across-g-gj-in-0-2-0-5-1-0-2-0-5-0-at-n-ap-120>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-4-chvykov-low-rattling-c4-breakdown-slope-at-alpha-0-90-with-exit-rates-fixed>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-4-chvykov-low-rattling-enrichment-p-ss-r-0-08-p-ss-r-1-25-alpha-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-4-chvykov-low-rattling-fitted-log-log-slope-of-p-ss-vs-r-exit-alpha-0>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-5-polycomputing-xor-and-or-truth-table-agreement-from-s-a-b>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-6-pigozzi-conditioning-cs-only-steady-us-activation-of-the-3-node-ode-before-after-paired-training>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-6-watson-natural-induction-single-epoch-delta-e-on-the-16-gene-target-eta-0-05>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-6-watson-natural-induction-target-attractor-basin-fraction-before-after-15-hebbian-epochs>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-7-causal-emergence-2-0-s-6-delta-cp-under-the-i-v-macro-swap-dynamics>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-8-multicellular-pd-exact-2d-square-lattice-internal-bond-fraction-m-5-k-25>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-8-multicellular-pd-viability-breakeven-defector-tie-strict-dominance-k-at-b-2-c-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-bib-dois-resolving-via-crossref-with-title-and-author-list-of-record>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-documented-outcome-values-that-disagree-with-the-code-s-output>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-laws-whose-python-evaluation-is-a-dynamical-linear-algebraic-or-combinatorial-computation-whose-asserted-outcome-is-not-fixed-by-construction>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-lean-theorems-binding-at-least-one-universally-quantified-parameter-that-appears-in-the-conclusion>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-math-kg-yaml-loci-that-start-at-the-declaration-definition-they-cite-and-lie-within-the-file>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-referee-attributed-measurement-records-in-the-kg-payload-whose-values-were-altered-by-the-builder>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-referee-count-stale-cross-artefact-references-loci-names-file-sections-remaining-after-the-pass-3-2-sweep>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-1>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-2>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-3>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-4>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-5>,
            <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-morphometric-validation-6> ;
        pk:hasScore "0.51"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-catalog-verification-cited-video-ids-resolving-in-the-374-video-catalog-with-sha-256-pin> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Catalog verification - cited video IDs resolving in the 374-video catalog, with SHA-256 pin = 63 ids_of_63" ;
        dct:description "Unchanged since Pass 3.1. No crawl or regeneration script is committed; the pinned mappedMathLaws labels still read 'Shreesha-Morozov-Levin' (L515)" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "set(law videos + concept videos) against videoId field (script L99-L118); reproduced; catalog SHA-256 216a474f... equals EXPECTED_CATALOG_SHA256 (L63) and README L9" ;
        schema:name "Catalog verification - cited video IDs resolving in the 374-video catalog, with SHA-256 pin" ;
        schema:unitText "ids_of_63" ;
        schema:value "63" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-catalog-verification-cited-video-ids-resolving-in-the-374-video-catalog-with-sha-256-pin-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-catalog-verification-cited-video-ids-resolving-in-the-374-video-catalog-with-sha-256-pin-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json (374 entries; 333.05 h)" ;
        schema:value "63" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-cli-expressivity-model-flags-that-complete-a-self-test-run-with-a-non-default-value> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "CLI expressivity - model flags that complete a --self-test run with a non-default value = 14 flags_of_14_tested" ;
        dct:description "Closes Pass 3.1 R6's abort (13 of 14 then). `--law` still runs all eight solvers and renders all six panels; it filters the output table only (L834-L836)" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Direct single invocations on 2026-10-25: --n-cells 50, --g-half 0.5, --g-half 5.0, --b 3, --b 1.2, --eta 0.01, --n-states 12, --gamma 2, --n-genes 8, --c 0.5, --v0 2, --v-th=-20, --seed 7, --law 2,4, --n-cells 20 --g-half 1.0, --delta-v-mv 0, --delta-v-mv -40: 17 of 17 invocations exit 0" ;
        schema:name "CLI expressivity - model flags that complete a --self-test run with a non-default value" ;
        schema:unitText "flags_of_14_tested" ;
        schema:value "14" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-bvp-spatial-reach-at-g-gj-1-0-n-100-g-half-0-1> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - BVP spatial reach at G_gj = 1.0, N = 100, G_half = 0.1 = 32.0099 cells" ;
        dct:description "1.6 % discrepancy is the discrete-vs-continuum correction. Physically this is the electrotonic space constant of a passive cable, lambda = sqrt(G/k); nothing in it is specific to TAME or to cognition" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "sum_i V_i / V_0 of the 100-cell steady state (script L186-L201); reproduced; G_gj = 0 gives 1.0, G_gj = 0.5 gives 22.8602. The law's metric (L728) and asserted quantity (L848-L849)" ;
        schema:name "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - BVP spatial reach at G_gj = 1.0, N = 100, G_half = 0.1" ;
        schema:unitText "cells" ;
        schema:value "32.0099" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-bvp-spatial-reach-at-g-gj-1-0-n-100-g-half-0-1-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-bvp-spatial-reach-at-g-gj-1-0-n-100-g-half-0-1-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "Continuum limit of the same diffusion-leak equation, sqrt(G/k) tanh(N sqrt(k/G)) with k = G_half/N = 0.001 (script L210; referee re-derivation of the closed form); no published reach exists in Levin (2019) Front. Psychol. 10:2688 or Levin (2022) Front. Syst. Neurosci. 16:768201" ;
        schema:value "31.5097" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-hill-form-1-n-1-g-g-g-eff-fitted-to-the-bvp-reach-curve-over-g-in-0-2-51-points-g-eff-and-rms-residual> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - Hill form 1 + (N - 1) G/(G + G_eff) fitted to the BVP reach curve over G in [0, 2] (51 points): G_eff and RMS residual = 2.26 conductance_units (G_eff); RMS 3.0478 cells" ;
        dct:description "Closes Pass 3.1 R2's unimplemented-fit finding. The fit also shows the Hill form is mis-specified for this model: the BVP reach has log-log slope 0.48 in G over (0, 2] and no plateau (44.19 cells at G = 2), the fitted half-saturation 2.26 lies outside the sweep, max |Hill - BVP| = 5.6 cells; the Lean theorem (L30-L60) formalises this Hill numerator, not the BVP" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Script L213-L216 (scipy.optimize.curve_fit, p0 = 1, bounds 1e-6..1e4): G_eff 2.26, fitted RMS 3.0478, unfitted (G_half = 0.1) RMS 55.1846; reproduced independently with scipy.optimize.minimize_scalar (bounded) on the RMS: G_eff 2.2600, RMS 3.0478" ;
        schema:name "Law 1 (TAME light cone) - Hill form 1 + (N - 1) G/(G + G_eff) fitted to the BVP reach curve over G in [0, 2] (51 points): G_eff and RMS residual" ;
        schema:unitText "conductance_units (G_eff); RMS 3.0478 cells" ;
        schema:value "2.26" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-hill-form-1-n-1-g-g-g-eff-fitted-to-the-bvp-reach-curve-over-g-in-0-2-51-points-g-eff-and-rms-residual-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-1-tame-light-cone-hill-form-1-n-1-g-g-g-eff-fitted-to-the-bvp-reach-curve-over-g-in-0-2-51-points-g-eff-and-rms-residual-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "Independent bounded 1-D least-squares minimisation by the referee of the same objective (not an external datum)" ;
        schema:value "2.26" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-bell-conductance-isolation-ratio-g-60-60-g-10-10-at-v-th-35-v-0-5> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 2 (Cervera gap junction) - Bell conductance isolation ratio G(-60,-60) / G(-10,-10) at V_th = -35, V_0 = 5 = 22026.47 dimensionless" ;
        dct:description "Exact agreement; verifies the implementation of the published G_ij form, not a measured quantity" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Script output bell_conductance_isolation_ratio; re-derived in closed form: (1 + e^5)^2 / (1 + e^-5)^2 = e^10 = 22026.4658" ;
        schema:name "Law 2 (Cervera gap junction) - Bell conductance isolation ratio G(-60,-60) / G(-10,-10) at V_th = -35, V_0 = 5" ;
        schema:unitText "dimensionless" ;
        schema:value "22026.47" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-bell-conductance-isolation-ratio-g-60-60-g-10-10-at-v-th-35-v-0-5-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-bell-conductance-isolation-ratio-g-60-60-g-10-10-at-v-th-35-v-0-5-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "Closed-form identity e^10 from the Bell-Boltzmann expression of Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020) for G_ij at symmetric V_i = V_j (referee derivation)" ;
        schema:value "22026.4658" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-healthy-tail-v-mem-bell-gated-vs-ohmic-control-t-80> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 2 (Cervera gap junction) - healthy-tail V_mem, Bell-gated vs ohmic control, t = 80 = -60.003 mV" ;
        dct:description "Genuine two-regime ODE outcome. Reference is model-internal (the chosen root), not Cervera's reported value" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "RK45 on the 20-cell chain, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV (script L239-L285, unchanged since Pass 3); reproduced. Ohmic control tail: -10.0 mV" ;
        schema:name "Law 2 (Cervera gap junction) - healthy-tail V_mem, Bell-gated vs ohmic control, t = 80" ;
        schema:unitText "mV" ;
        schema:value "-60.003" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-healthy-tail-v-mem-bell-gated-vs-ohmic-control-t-80-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-2-cervera-gap-junction-healthy-tail-v-mem-bell-gated-vs-ohmic-control-t-80-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "Polarised stable root of the script's own cubic I_ion; Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020) J. Phys. Chem. Lett. 11:3234 report isolation of depolarised domains qualitatively, no published tail voltage is compared" ;
        schema:value "-60.0" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-absolute-error-of-c-post-c-ant-vs-exp-dv-v-t-across-n-ap-15-30-60-120-240> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 3 (Pietak-Levin Nernst-Planck) - absolute error of c_post / c_ant vs exp(dV/V_T) across N_ap = 15, 30, 60, 120, 240 = 2.5e-05 dimensionless (at N_ap = 240)" ;
        dct:description "Genuine convergence check. `--delta-v-mv 0` now completes (guard at L853): all five errors are exactly 0 and the strict test is skipped" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Script abs_errors_by_grid = [0.007422, 0.001726, 0.000417, 0.000102, 0.000025]; successive ratios 4.30, 4.14, 4.09, 4.08 (referee), consistent with O(h^2)" ;
        schema:name "Law 3 (Pietak-Levin Nernst-Planck) - absolute error of c_post / c_ant vs exp(dV/V_T) across N_ap = 15, 30, 60, 120, 240" ;
        schema:unitText "dimensionless (at N_ap = 240)" ;
        schema:value "2.5e-05" ;
        schema:valueReference <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-absolute-error-of-c-post-c-ant-vs-exp-dv-v-t-across-n-ap-15-30-60-120-240-reference> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-absolute-error-of-c-post-c-ant-vs-exp-dv-v-t-across-n-ap-15-30-60-120-240-reference> a schema:PropertyValue ;
        dct:source "Expected error ratio per grid doubling for a second-order scheme (standard numerical-analysis result; referee check of the O(h^2) claim at script L296-L298)" ;
        schema:value "4.0" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-measurement-law-3-pietak-levin-nernst-planck-central-difference-c-post-c-ant-at-dv-40-mv-n-ap-120-g-gj-1-0> a schema:PropertyValue,
            pk:EvidenceItem ;
        rdfs:label "Law 3 (Pietak-Levin Nernst-Planck) - central-difference c_post / c_ant at dV = 40 mV, N_ap = 120, G_gj = 1.0 = 4.699286 dimensionless" ;
        dct:description "Agreement is a convergence result, not a construction: the edge ratio (1 - dv/2)/(1 + dv/2) differs from exp(-dv) at O(dv^3)" ;
        schema:measurementTechnique "Solve of the Pade(1,1) / central-difference flux-balance BVP (script L301-L317); reproduced; relative error 2.18e-5 (0.00218 %)" ;
        schema:name "Law 3 (Pietak-Levin Nernst-Planck) - central-difference c_post / c_ant at dV = 40 mV, N_ap = 120, G_gj = 1.0" ;
        schema:unitText "dimensionless" ;
